[preflight] snapshot 6 files from assets/ReCodeAgent/data/tool_projects/crust/amp/c
[delegate] analyst <- Analyze the source codebase, identify all modules, dependencies, and entry points, and produce a source map and brief in meta/plan.md.
[phase] Contract
[delegate] architect <- Produce the target-language contract in analysis/brief.md from analysis/source-map.md: define the public API surface (amp_encode/amp_decode/amp_decode_arg, amp_t, AMP_VERSION), the target-language data types and ownership model replacing raw char* and pointer-cursor arithmetic, the VLA and fixed-width-short replacements, bit-packing and memcpy strategy, and the error/assert handling approach, so a validator can check it.
[delegate] validator <- Validate the C->Rust migration contract in analysis/brief.md against the 8 frozen contracts it defines (frozen public API surface: AMP_VERSION, Amp struct, amp_encode/amp_decode/amp_decode_arg; Rust ownership model replacing raw char*/pointer-cursor arithmetic; VLA->Vec, memcpy->slice copy, short->u16, assert->assert!, bit-packing on u8; target layout lib.rs + tests/roundtrip.rs + Cargo.toml; test strategy). Confirm each contract is concrete and checkable, flag any ambiguity or gap, and report pass/fail per contract.
[phase] Planning
[delegate] planner <- Read analysis/brief.md (the validated C->Rust contract) and analysis/source-map.md, and produce the migration batch plan in meta/plan.md: partition the target (Cargo.toml, lib.rs with the Amp struct + amp_encode/amp_decode/amp_decode_arg, and tests/roundtrip.rs plus the 4 characterization tests) into the smallest set of ordered batches such that every target module is in exactly one batch and each batch's dependencies are satisfied by earlier batches (batch order compiles). For each batch list: the files it owns, the frozen contracts it must satisfy, its acceptance/exit check, and the exact order to execute. Keep the plan consistent with the 8 frozen contracts and the no-unsafe / no-external-deps constraints.
[phase] Pilot
[delegate] translator <- Implement Batch 1 of the migration plan (meta/plan.md) in the target workspace: create target/Cargo.toml (package name/version/description from source/package.json, edition = "2021", and NO [dependencies] section or an empty one) and target/src/lib.rs containing ONLY the library body (do NOT add the #[cfg(test)] module — that is Batch 2). In lib.rs, in this leaf-first order: (1) pub const AMP_VERSION: u8 = 1; (2) pub struct Amp { pub version: u16, pub argc: u16, buf: Vec<u8>, pos: usize }; (3) private helpers fn read_u32_be(buf: &[u8], pos: usize) -> u32 and fn write_u32_be(val: u32, buf: &mut [u8], pos: usize) (NOT pub); (4) pub fn amp_decode(msg: &mut Amp, buf: &[u8]) that sets version from the high nibble and argc from the low nibble of buf[0], sets pos = 1, and performs no allocation; (5) pub fn amp_decode_arg(msg: &mut Amp) -> Vec<u8> that reads the 4-byte big-endian length at pos, copies buf[pos..pos+len] into a new Vec<u8>, advances pos, and does not mutate buf contents; (6) pub fn amp_encode(argv: &[&str], argc: usize) -> Vec<u8> that emits one header byte (AMP_VERSION << 4 | argc) then, per arg, a 4-byte big-endian length followed by the arg bytes, using Vec<u32>/Vec<u8> (no VLA) and extend_from_slice (no memcpy). Hard constraints: the public surface must be EXACTLY AMP_VERSION, Amp, amp_encode, amp_decode, amp_decode_arg (helpers stay private); zero occurrences of `unsafe` anywhere under target/; no external crate dependencies. Acceptance: `cargo build` in target/ succeeds with no warnings, grep of target/ for `unsafe` returns zero matches, and Cargo.toml has no [dependencies]. Report the build result and the public-name list when done.
[delegate] tester <- Implement Batch 2 of the migration plan (meta/plan.md) in the target workspace: (1) create target/tests/roundtrip.rs translating the C round-trip test — encode 3 args ("some", "stuff", "here") with amp_encode, amp_decode the header into an Amp, assert version == 1 and argc == 3, then make 3 successive amp_decode_arg calls and assert each returns the original arg bytes in order; (2) append a #[cfg(test)] mod tests block to target/src/lib.rs containing exactly 4 characterization tests that pin the wire format: (a) amp_encode output for a known argv matches the exact expected byte sequence (header byte then 4-byte big-endian length + arg bytes per arg), (b) amp_decode + amp_decode_arg is the inverse of amp_encode (round-trip recovers each arg), (c) read_u32_be/write_u32_be round-trip a known u32 value, and (d) amp_encode with argc == 0 yields a single header byte (AMP_VERSION << 4 | 0) and amp_decode reports argc == 0. Hard constraints: do NOT change the public surface (still exactly AMP_VERSION, Amp, amp_encode, amp_decode, amp_decode_arg); zero occurrences of `unsafe` anywhere under target/; no external crate dependencies (Cargo.toml unchanged, no [dependencies]). Acceptance: `cargo build` and `cargo test` in target/ both succeed with no warnings, all 5 tests (1 integration + 4 characterization) pass, grep of target/ for `unsafe` returns zero matches, and the public-name list is unchanged. Report the `cargo test` result and the test names when done.
[phase] Migration
